{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">
    Don't ask a model for JSON in plain prose and hope it formats it right. Use structured output so the response is guaranteed to parse.
  </div>
        <div class="tone-mid">
    A JSON schema constrains the model's output at generation time, removing the need for regex extraction or a parse-retry loop.
  </div>
        <div class="tone-staff">
    Schema conformance guarantees shape, not correctness. Validate semantic constraints (real data source, sane values) separately from parsing.
  </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
